  "laws": [
    "Capability identity survives implementation succession.",
    "Substrate succession cannot change capability semantics, authority, work-class scope, or evidence obligations.",
    "The reconciler observes and proposes; it never promotes or activates.",
    "Hardening proceeds one admitted substrate rung at a time.",
    "A non-inference occupancy retains an admitted inference-capable fallback.",
    "Residual uncertainty is routed upward, never hidden inside a deterministic claim.",
    "Candidate equivalence requires evidence authored independently of the candidate author.",
    "Institutional obligations are idempotent across changing evidence windows; each observed decision may still produce distinct evidence.",
    "Contradiction, drift, workaround, or excess uncertainty may propose softening.",
    "A profile from a stale occupancy or implementation cannot drive succession.",
    "Promotion economics are decided from independently observed cost, quality, latency, cognition fraction, and evidence; candidate forecasts are not admission evidence.",
    "A transition proposal names the exact source occupancy and exact target implementation strategy.",
    "A work profile from the future, without a distribution identity, or without evidence references cannot drive hardening.",
    "All substrates are digital; hardware terminology is analogy only.",
    "Learning policy identity and revision are bound to every construction, evaluation, and transition obligation.",
    "Work profiles bind the exact capability revision, work class, occupancy, and implementation they measured.",
    "Equivalence assessments bind the exact candidate revision, work profile, and equivalence contract they evaluated.",
    "Fixed substrate means zero runtime cognition inside the admitted work-class contract.",
    "Candidate lifecycle, occupancy status, substrate, and epistemic state are independent dimensions.",
    "The learning policy substrate list is a contiguous prefix of inference, configuration, fixed.",
    "Inference occupancy has cognition fraction 1; configuration reduces it; fixed has cognition fraction 0.",
    "Assessment cannot predate either the candidate or the work profile it evaluates.",
    "A zero-cost baseline cannot produce a positive savings ratio.",
    "A changed learning-policy revision creates a new institutional obligation."
  ],
  "heartime_summary": {
